# Feature Module Conventions

## Directory Structure

```
features/{name}/src/main/kotlin/.../feature/{name}/
├── data/              ← Feature-local repository/data source (optional, rare)
├── di/                ← Feature-level Hilt modules
├── domain/            ← Feature-specific use cases (optional)
├── presentation/
│   ├── components/    ← Small composable building blocks
│   ├── model/         ← UIState data classes, UI-only models
│   ├── navigation/    ← Route definition + NavGraphBuilder extension
│   ├── {Name}Screen.kt
│   ├── {Name}Routing.kt  ← Wires ViewModel → Screen (hiltViewModel)
│   └── {Name}ViewModel.kt
```

## ViewModel

```kotlin
@HiltViewModel
class DashboardViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val getWalletSummaryUseCase: GetWalletSummaryUseCase,
    private val dispatcher: CommonDispatcher,
) : ViewModel() {

    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow(DashboardUIState())
    val uiState: StateFlow<DashboardUIState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()

    init {
        viewModelScope.launch(dispatcher.io) { loadData() }
    }
}
```

Rules:
- `@HiltViewModel` + `@Inject constructor`
- Expose `StateFlow<UIState>` — never expose `MutableStateFlow`
- Use `CommonDispatcher` (not hardcoded `Dispatchers.IO`)
- Prefer use cases over direct repository calls
- Never hold `Context` — use `@ApplicationContext` only if absolutely needed

## UI State

```kotlin
data class DashboardUIState(
    val isLoading: Boolean = false,
    val walletSummary: WalletSummary? = null,
    val recentTransactions: List<Transaction> = emptyList(),
    val error: String? = null,
)
```

Rules:
- Single data class per screen — all UI state in one place
- Sensible defaults (empty lists, false, null)
- Sealed class variants for distinct screen states are also acceptable

## Screen + Routing Pattern

```kotlin
// {Name}Routing.kt — wiring layer
@Composable
fun DashboardRouting(viewModel: DashboardViewModel = hiltViewModel()) {
    val uiState by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()
    DashboardScreen(uiState = uiState, onAction = viewModel::handleAction)
}

// {Name}Screen.kt — pure composable (no ViewModel dependency)
@Composable
fun DashboardScreen(uiState: DashboardUIState, onAction: (Action) -> Unit) { ... }
```

Rules:
- Screen composable is stateless — receives state + callbacks
- Routing composable connects ViewModel → Screen
- Screen must have `@Preview` annotations (light and dark)
- Use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` (not `collectAsState()`)

## Navigation

```kotlin
// Route definition
@Serializable
object DashboardRoute

// NavGraphBuilder extension
fun NavGraphBuilder.dashboardGraph() {
    composable<DashboardRoute> { DashboardRouting() }
}

// Navigate extension (if needed)
fun NavController.navigateToDashboard(navOptions: NavOptions? = null) {
    navigate(DashboardRoute, navOptions)
}
```

Rules:
- Routes are `@Serializable object` (type-safe navigation)
- Each feature exposes a `NavGraphBuilder.{name}Graph()` extension
- Navigation functions go in `navigation/` package
- The `:app` module orchestrates all feature graphs in `KeuTrackNavHost`

## Compose

- Use `KeuTrackTheme` for all `@Preview` — never bare `MaterialTheme`
- Use Material 2 (`androidx.compose.material`) — the project does not use Material 3
- Extract reusable components to `components/` sub-package
- Prefix project-wide components with `KeuTrack` (e.g., `KeuTrackButton`)
